  "type": "credits",
  "name": "Waves victory",
  "notes": "ALL WAVES CLEARED! over the meadow sky, with the winning monster bobbing, the final time, level and kills. The run's time is checked against this monster's best waves time (best_time[entry]): if it never won a waves run before, or this run was faster, it becomes the new best and the screen says NEW BEST TIME! with a jingle, otherwise it shows the best time to beat. The best time is saved at once. Waves wins unlock nothing. Every 5 different runs won make a monster shiny (the 18 menu entries, 9 classic and 9 waves runs, each count once until the next shiny; winning the same run again counts nothing): on the 5th, this screen picks the winner if it isn't shiny yet, otherwise a random monster that isn't (new_shiny), never one twice, until all 9 shine. It only picks: the shiny screen (scn_shiny), after the items screen, makes it shiny and saves. A winner that already was shiny shimmers here too. Every win also gives 3 items for the next run, picked at random, never the same one twice (3 different of the 5 floor items: prize_1-3), replacing any not used yet, and saves them with the rest; START opens the items screen (scn_prizes), which shows them and then goes on to the shiny screen or the menu.",
